      "content": "Wait, it looks like the message cut off at the very end. Must have been a glitch.\n\nAlso, looking at the draft, the word count is still looking a bit low for what the system expects. If we can't get it closer to that 500-600 range, it's going to be a pain to go through the manual review process. \n\nCan you finish that thought and beef up the whole guide a bit more? You could add a \"Prerequisites\" section at the start, maybe a \"Troubleshooting\" part at the end, or just go into more depth about the architecture. Just please, try to make it meaningful—I don't want it to look like we're just padding the text to trick the metric, but we definitely need the length to pass the automated check.",
